WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.544
Passive monitoring observes existing communication without sending probes or commands to the monitored devices.

00:00:05.544 --> 00:00:10.600
This approach is often preferred in OT because some legacy controllers, protocol stacks,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.711
and embedded devices are sensitive to unexpected traffic.

00:00:13.711 --> 00:00:17.600
Visibility should not create an avoidable production or safety risk.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.266
A network tap can provide a copy of traffic while remaining electrically

00:00:22.266 --> 00:00:24.211
isolated from the monitored path.

00:00:24.211 --> 00:00:29.655
A switch SPAN or mirror port can also copy selected traffic to a sensor,

00:00:29.655 --> 00:00:33.155
though configuration, capacity, and switch behavior must be reviewed.

00:00:33.155 --> 00:00:37.821
Sensors should be placed where they can observe meaningful flows without becoming

00:00:37.821 --> 00:00:39.766
part of the control path.

00:00:39.766 --> 00:00:43.266
Passive collection can identify devices, protocols, communication pairs, timing,

00:00:43.266 --> 00:00:44.821
and some command types.

00:00:44.821 --> 00:00:48.321
It is particularly useful around control-area boundaries, industrial DMZs,

00:00:48.321 --> 00:00:52.210
remote-access gateways, and links between site operations and lower-level networks.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:53.765
Passive monitoring has limits.

00:00:53.765 --> 00:00:57.654
It may not see dormant assets, serial networks, encrypted content,

00:00:57.654 --> 00:01:02.710
traffic on an unobserved switch, or activity that occurs entirely within a device.

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:05.821
Asset inventory, host logs, vendor records, configuration review,

00:01:05.821 --> 00:01:07.765
and physical verification remain necessary.

00:01:07.765 --> 00:01:09.321
Deployment requires engineering coordination.

00:01:09.321 --> 00:01:12.043
Confirm that taps, mirror ports, sensors, power,

00:01:12.043 --> 00:01:15.932
and management connections do not interfere with redundancy or timing.

00:01:15.932 --> 00:01:19.432
Secure the monitoring platform itself, separate its management path,

00:01:19.432 --> 00:01:24.098
restrict access to captured data, and define what happens if collection stops.

00:01:24.098 --> 00:01:27.209
The principle is observe safely and interpret carefully.

00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:29.154
Passive evidence reduces blind spots,

00:01:29.154 --> 00:01:33.820
but it does not automatically prove that an asset is secure or

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.765
that every action is authorized.

00:01:35.765 --> 00:01:38.876
Monitoring becomes reliable when its coverage, limitations, ownership,

00:01:38.876 --> 00:01:40.820
and operational assumptions are documented.
